cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "galform_execution"
abstract: >
  A Python package and command-line tool for generating and submitting
  GALFORM semi-analytic galaxy formation runs on N-body merger trees to
  SLURM on the COSMA HPC cluster. It builds the job scripts, injects
  simulation and model parameters into GALFORM .input.ref files, packs all
  subvolumes of a snapshot into a single SLURM slot, and controls the
  post-processing stages (NETA, luminosity functions, stellar mass functions).
